**java.util.concurrent.atomic**

Inka main kaam hai thread-safe operations bina heavy synchronized lock lagaye.
Matlab multiple threads ek hi data ko update karein aur data corrupt na ho.

“Atomic” = operation ya to pura hoga ya bilkul nahi hoga.
Beech me koi thread ghus ke value kharab nahi karega.


Classes

AtomicBoolean  = Boolean ko thread-safe banana.

AtomicInteger  = Thread-safe integer counter.
AtomicIntergerArray = Array ke individual elements ko thread-safe banana

AtomicLong       = Same as AtomicInteger but for huge numbers.
AtomicLongArray  = Array ke individual elements ko thread-safe banana

AtomicReference = Object reference ko atomically replace karna.
AtomicReferenceArray = Array ke individual elements ko thread-safe banana

AtomicStampedReference = Reference + integer version/stamp. Ye bahut important hai.

DoubleAdder = Same as LongAdder but for double values.
 DoubleAccumulator

LongAdder = Ye modern high-performance counter hai. Heavy concurrent counting
AtomicLong me sab threads ek hi variable pe fight karte hain.
LongAdder internally multiple counters use karta hai.
Traffic divide ho jata hai.

LongAccumulator = Custom operation with long.

